("I was twenty-two when I walked into my first classroom in Jaipur. Thirty-five pairs of eyes looking at me,) Tj
T* (expecting wisdom. I was terrified! My hands were shaking as I wrote my name on the blackboard. Then a) Tj
T* (little girl in the front row smiled at me—her two front teeth were missing. That smile gave me courage. I) Tj
T* (taught for forty years after that day, and I never forgot that little girl's gift.") Tj
