("It was at a wedding in Delhi, 1960. I was supposed to be watching the ceremony, but I kept looking at this) Tj
T* (young woman across the room. She caught me staring and didn't look away. My friend nudged me: 'That's) Tj
T* (the schoolteacher everyone's talking about. Very educated. Too smart for you!' I walked up to her anyway.) Tj
T* (The first thing she said was, 'You're blocking my view of the bride.' I said, 'Then I'll be your view instead.') Tj
T* (She laughed, and I was lost forever.") Tj
