("I was doing my medical residency in London, 1992. It was pouring rain, and I'd forgotten my) Tj
T* (umbrella—again. I ducked into a jazz club to escape the downpour. A man was playing saxophone on stage,) Tj
T* (eyes closed, lost in the music. When he opened his eyes, he looked right at me standing there, dripping wet,) Tj
T* (and smiled without missing a note. After the show, he came over and said, 'You look like you need some) Tj
T* (sunshine.' I said, 'You sound like sunshine.' James still plays that song he was playing when we met. He calls) Tj
T* (it 'Rain in Delhi.'") Tj
