("When I was fifteen, I spent a summer in Jaipur with Nani. One afternoon, she pulled out a tin box full of old) Tj
T* (photographs I'd never seen. There was Nana as a young man, standing proudly by a bridge. Mom as a little) Tj
T* (girl, eating ice cream with sticky hands. And a black and white photo of people I didn't recognize. 'Who are) Tj
T* (they, Nani?' She went quiet. 'People we lost during Partition. This is why we tell stories, beta. So they are) Tj
T* (never truly gone.' That summer, I decided to become a filmmaker. To make sure no story is ever lost.") Tj
ET
