("Last year, Nana had a stroke. For three days, he couldn't speak. I sat by his bed, terrified that all his) Tj
T* (stories—the bridges, old Delhi, how he met Nani—would disappear with him. When he recovered, the first) Tj
T* (thing he said was, 'Did I ever tell you about the river at Haridwar?' I started recording that same day. Every) Tj
T* (story, every voice, every detail. That's when I knew I had to build something for all families, not just ours. So) Tj
T* (that no one has to fear losing the voices they love.") Tj
ET
