("In 1975, I was assigned to build a bridge over the Ganges at Haridwar. Engineers said the current was too) Tj
T* (strong, the river too sacred to tame. But I spent weeks watching the water, learning its moods. One morning,) Tj
T* (an old priest told me, 'Don't fight the river, son. Dance with it.' That bridge still stands today. I take my) Tj
T* (grandchildren there and tell them: respect what you cannot control, and you'll find a way.") Tj
